# iOS code-signing material — NEVER commit. The .p12 + private_key.pem are
# permanent credentials that, if leaked, let anyone sign apps as "Apple
# Distribution: Guidion Sama". Apple has no recovery — only revocation +
# re-issue. The whole scripts/_ios_signing/ directory is local-only.
scripts/_ios_signing/
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
private_key.pem
*_base64.txt

# Webhook secrets — NEVER commit a file that contains SCRIPT_SECRET,
# the Apps Script shared key that authenticates apply_contributions.py
# to the privileged endpoints (approve/reject/fetch_audio). If leaked,
# anyone can approve their own malicious contributions.
#
# config/webhooks.json IS tracked because Flutter bundles it as an asset
# (pubspec.yaml -> assets) so the running app knows which URL to call.
# It contains ONLY the public webhook URLs (the URLs themselves return
# `unauthorized` to anyone without a valid Firebase ID token / secret).
# DO NOT add `script_secret` to that file — keep the secret in the
# AWING_SCRIPT_SECRET env var or ~/.awing_script_secret instead.
.awing_script_secret

# Play Console + App Store Connect credentials for
# scripts/check_version_codes.py. Private — service-account JSON / .p8
# keys that grant API access to the same Play / ASC orgs CI uses for
# upload. Never commit. CI uses its own secrets (PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON,
# ASC_KEY_ID / ASC_ISSUER_ID / ASC_KEY_BASE64); these files are the
# LOCAL equivalent for running the pre-tag version check from your dev
# machine. config/webhooks.json above remains tracked — those URLs are
# public.
config/play-service-account.json
config/asc-credentials.json
config/*.p8

# IntelliJ related
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# The .vscode folder contains launch configuration and tasks you configure in
# VS Code which you may wish to be included in version control, so this line
# is commented out by default.
#.vscode/

# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
# v1.23.6 (Session 65c): no trailing slash. These are now NTFS junctions
# (see scripts/ensure_local_build_dirs.ps1 - the build tree lives outside
# OneDrive), and git reports a junction as a SYMLINK, not a directory. A
# trailing-slash pattern matches directories only, so `.dart_tool/` stopped
# matching and both paths reappeared as untracked.
.dart_tool
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/build
/coverage/

